ially been given the  green light there ought to be new  details soon  it's not getting any quieter at DC these  days only last week reports about the  plant restructuring of the dceu caused  quite a stir in Hollywood the list of  affected projects is long for instance  Wonder Woman 3 Black Adam 2 and Aquaman  3 will be canceled the idea is to create  a completely new universe that is no  longer connected to the so-called  snyderverse equally affected was Man of  Steel 2 which ironically was even teased  at the end of Black Adam this will have  been the last appearance of Henry Cavill  in his popular role as he now confirmed  in an official statement thus Peter  Safran and James Gunn the two heads of  DC Studios have met him and presented  him their plans he himself respects the  decision of the two after all they must  also create a completely new universe  but still it is not easy for him on the  other hand it has to be pointed out that  gun and saffron only recently took over  their positions as creative directors of  DC which is why they are only partly to  blame for the chaotic back and forth  nevertheless one thing is certain there  are plans for Superman in the upcoming  dceu as gun announced almost  simultaneously with cattle statement in  contrast to a Man of Steel 2 there will  be a kind of prequel that shows the  superhero in his younger years Gunn  himself will write the corresponding  script and possibly also take over the  directing despite the disappointment  that many fans of Henry Cavill surely  feel the new project does at least raise  some curiosity whatever the outcome we  will keep you up to date on further news  last year Dennis Villa nueva's Dune won  six Academy Awards out of 10 nominations  outshining all of its competitors the  Epic film is based on the 1965 book by  Frank Herbert and revolves around young  Paul Atreides who finds himself in a  confusing situation that not only takes  his father's life but also forces the  ruling a triades 